{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively","id":1155342,"title":"I'm worried that the Fate Arcana is too potent, whether mechanically or narratively","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-03T04:15:09-07:00","id":1155342,"title":"I'm worried that the Fate Arcana is too potent, whether mechanically or narratively","content":"So as the title states, I've been having a lot of issues with the Fate Arcana in a lot of ways, most of which really stem from a few facts, mainly its diversity, and its raw power when it comes to both pure mechanical effects like dice pools, and it's narrative impact in directing the story.<br /> <br /> I truly struggle to imagine many scenarios fate could not cover, given its broad purview and potent effects. A mage with a sanctum and downtime could bring the world down around him and buff himself above even gods. In addition to blanket access to destiny and probability manipulation and anti-mind and destiny effects (destiny effects also being highly likely to contest time magic too), it seems like an all too potent magic with very few weaknesses. <br /> <br /> Further, these weaknesses feel like they can easily be shored up even by a novice mage with the right intent. 2 prime and the infinite recursive dice bonuses put into wards and signs and a veil, and things get quite difficult. <br /> <br /> Basically I'm looking for some help changing my mind and position regarding Fate being too broad and too impactful, although I won't hide the fact that my position is somewhat entrenched. I do hope that some discourse and posts will shed light on aspects I've failed to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T04:25:43-07:00","id":1155345,"title":"","content":"Infinite recursive loop actually isn\u2019t infinite.<br /> <br /> Spirit and Mind could be argued to be just as broken considering how dependent people are on their minds and that there\u2019s a spirit for everything. I could make similar arguments for the other arcana as well. Long story short, yes, Fate is powerful, but no it\u2019s not broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-03-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T04:58:50-07:00","id":1155350,"title":"","content":"I'd love to be shown my error regarding its infinite use. I do recall threads on it, and most can't decide if boons can grant bonus dice, from what I could tell, considering the book section and exceptional luck contradicted slightly. The spell itself is Exceptional Luck, yea? It's clearly written to let you Grant yourself conditions and dice bonuses and apply them to spellcasting, barring a house rule I'd gladly accept. Even if you don't allow it to stack one casting onto another you still have the exceptionally strange effect of allowing Fate to improve spellcasting at a rate better than even Prime? <br /> <br /> Also, while I do agree with the potential power of spirit, I unfortunately feel that much if what mind can do is too easily mimicked, or at least the same end goal reached, with other Arcana, one of which is absolutely Fate, imo. You can't read minds or change emotions or rewire beliefs directly, but you can manage those end results just about the same. <br /> <br /> I suppose a further issue is how vague &quot;destiny&quot; is when referred to as part of fate spells, because it is clearly something beyond just the merit itself. Still I appreciate the input and am inclined to agree with the potential of spirit, although I find it easier to imagine its uses and counters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":".  Spelling 11-03-2017, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T05:15:53-07:00","id":1155352,"title":"","content":"Each iteration grants less and less dice until it's unlikely to grant more dice than you've already amassed. It's theoretically possible (but definitely practically impossible) to gain infinite dice, but only because the dice are exploding; not because of the recursive loop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:01:47-07:00","id":1155391,"title":"","content":"For my game, I pointed players to the general guide on hexes and boons on page 134 to determine which ones applied to spellcasting. The powergaming acanthus was reigned in, but still had plenty to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:25:40-07:00","id":1155404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1155350#post1155350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you don't allow it to stack one casting onto another you still have the exceptionally strange effect of allowing Fate to improve spellcasting at a rate better than even Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the firm opinion that that's a solid indicator of the guideline for Boons and Hexes at the start of the Arcanum writeup not being superceded by the lack of specificity in the spell's Reach option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:25:24-08:00","id":1156291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1155350#post1155350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to be shown my error regarding its infinite use. I do recall threads on it, and most can't decide if boons can grant bonus dice, from what I could tell, considering the book section and exceptional luck contradicted slightly. The spell itself is Exceptional Luck, yea? It's clearly written to let you Grant yourself conditions and dice bonuses and apply them to spellcasting, barring a house rule I'd gladly accept. Even if you don't allow it to stack one casting onto another you still have the exceptionally strange effect of allowing Fate to improve spellcasting at a rate better than even Prime?<br /> <br /> Also, while I do agree with the potential power of spirit, I unfortunately feel that much if what mind can do is too easily mimicked, or at least the same end goal reached, with other Arcana, one of which is absolutely Fate, imo. You can't read minds or change emotions or rewire beliefs directly, but you can manage those end results just about the same.<br /> <br /> I suppose a further issue is how vague &quot;destiny&quot; is when referred to as part of fate spells, because it is clearly something beyond just the merit itself. Still I appreciate the input and am inclined to agree with the potential of spirit, although I find it easier to imagine its uses and counters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you remembering that each time you exceed the +5 bonus that it costs a point of mana? I remember discussing Exceptional luck and Monkey paw <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page94\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page94</a> here and i think i came to the conclusion that you can cast for 4-5 times for a max bonus of around +16 dice, It cost about 6+ turns of casting, 3 mana and 3 willpower, with 2 paradox rolls. Each time you increase that Exceptional luck potency by 1 its costing you -2 penalty and your needing the informed condition to make that -5 chance dice spell to succeed.<br /> <br /> Also remember a high potency wards and signs spell is only 1 Exceptional Success away from being ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-06-2017, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:40:21-08:00","id":1156300,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a rule that explicitly stated rules such as that Informed and Steadfast didn't applied to spellcasting? Or at least not combined?<br /> <br /> Cuz then any mage could take those as their Nimbus conditions and spam them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 11-06-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:50:09-08:00","id":1156306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156300#post1156300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule that explicitly stated rules such as that Informed and Steadfast didn't applied to spellcasting? Or at least not combined?<br /> <br /> Cuz then any mage could take those as their Nimbus conditions and spam them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's probably the intent of the rules. Not sure if stated as it though. But automatic success on spellcasting seems &quot;a bit&quot; broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:12:29-08:00","id":1156316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156300#post1156300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cuz then any mage could take those as their Nimbus conditions and spam them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nimbus doesn\u2019t give Conditions, it applies a Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:54:33-08:00","id":1156346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156300#post1156300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule that explicitly stated rules such as that Informed and Steadfast didn't applied to spellcasting? Or at least not combined?<br /> <br /> Cuz then any mage could take those as their Nimbus conditions and spam them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Informed mentions any skill roll and spell casting isnt a skill roll. Steadfast and Inspired just mention an action or a roll. However Exceptional lucks reach effects says the boon can affect spell casting and considering exceptional successes can give arcane conditions that there arnt specific examples off, there is nothing saying you couldnt give yourself a Informed+ condition that works on spell casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:58:41-08:00","id":1156348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156346#post1156346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Informed mentions any skill roll and spell casting isnt a skill roll. Steadfast and Inspired just mention an action or a roll. However Exceptional lucks reach effects says the boon can affect spell casting and considering exceptional successes can give arcane conditions that there arnt specific examples off, there is nothing saying you couldnt give yourself a Informed+ condition that works on spell casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which returns us to the topic at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:07:11-08:00","id":1156350,"title":"","content":"The original topic was that fate is OP esp being able to abuse Exceptional Luck for massive amounts of extra dice, however if its not possible to use the informed condition on spellcasting the chances of getting a decent amount of extra dice from EL is vastly lowered or you have to roll a chance dice 4-5 times and succeed every time.<br /> <br /> I cant really comment on the other things the OP mentions, as any narrative impact it has on stories is left in individual ST's hands, some might let PC's get away with stuff using Fate i wouldnt and we cant list every example.<br /> <br /> The op does mention anti mind effects, not quite sure what they mean by this..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-06-2017, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:29:37-08:00","id":1156353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156350#post1156350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The op does mention anti mind effects, not quite sure what they mean by this..</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Fate effects that counter mind control effects as they impede your \u201cdestiny\u201d as determined by your own will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:05:10-08:00","id":1156367,"title":"","content":"So if we assume that EL can be used for spell casting, what's the biggest bonus you can get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:08:41-08:00","id":1156369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156367#post1156367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we assume that EL can be used for spell casting, what's the biggest bonus you can get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the thread i posted earlier, i did a quick example, i think i got up to +16 dice before i hit a limit. And that was using informed condition gained via EL to make each chance roll succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:16:05-08:00","id":1156371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156353#post1156353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are Fate effects that counter mind control effects as they impede your \u201cdestiny\u201d as determined by your own will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sword oath allowing a clash vs a mind control effect to break the oath? Personally dont see that as a OP part of fate, its very limited in scope probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:48:46-08:00","id":1156377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156371#post1156371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sword oath allowing a clash vs a mind control effect to break the oath? Personally dont see that as a OP part of fate, its very limited in scope probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warding Gesture also protects against mind control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T10:31:05-08:00","id":1156391,"title":"","content":"Fate can protect against overt mind control, which is fine to me. Every Mastigos knows that when messing with an Acanthus you use the carrot (illusions, changing their emotional responses, creating conditions that make them want certain things) instead of the stick (DO THIS NOW!)-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:04:52-08:00","id":1156425,"title":"","content":"I re-read the example. Personally, I wouldn't allow spamming Informed for spell casting. I'd maybe allow it for one roll if someone received it while doing some research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:46:33-08:00","id":1156441,"title":"","content":"I similarly say the dice bonus can't be applied to spellcasting with regards to boons, and just let them use the guide in the hex/boon writeup.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I personally agree that Fate can be pretty overpowered even among other mages; a large majority of its effects break many of the CT rules for what level is generally able to do what effects (creating tilts from nothing, for instance), and the Charmed condition is in and of itself far too potent, especially when you can do a large amount of other things in the same casting.<br /> <br /> One way to help might be to split the Boons/Hexes into separate effects (meaning a different rote for different types of boons for a given spell effect), or removing the condition/tilt options altogether and reintroducing it later as a more advanced effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:31:16-08:00","id":1156461,"title":"","content":"So i made afew mistakes in that EL example, one being forgetting the base 3 potency and another forgetting with a rote your within your free reaches. But assuming you cant use informed and you want to keep postive dice for spellcasting and El works on spellcasting, you still get up to +20 dice before diminishing returns start to kick in.<br /> <br /> Assuming base dicepool of 16 (Gnosis 3, Arcana 3, Mudra +4, High Speech +2, Tool + 1, Willpower + 3) thats only a initial EL spell with a potency of 10 (base 3 + 7 potency for -14) leaving a casting pool of 2 dice. You can keep going but each time you only get 1-4 dicepool, spend a mana, willpower, take 3 turns per roll and once you reach a total dicepool of 35 the -34 penalty for + 17(20 total) means your dicepool is 36 which is still only enough room for another -34 penalty and still having a dice to roll.<br /> <br /> If you want to spend 15+ turns, 5 mana, 5 willpower to give your next damage spell potency 20 good for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-06-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:19:42-08:00","id":1156475,"title":"","content":"Well it's your next 20 Spells, you can easily prepare it in less than a minute ingame time at say the start of the day and allmost guranteedly get the willpower and mana back (and more if you want to) by getting 5 exceptional successes by using some of the boon on less potency intensive spells.<br /> <br /> But I'm not here to argue. Personally I also don't allow spells to add dice to spellcasting or clashes of wills in any way. Whatever floats your boat though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T18:53:39-08:00","id":1156536,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest problem with Exceptional Luck is that the Informed Condition seems to be an easy way to short circuit any (lower-case) mystery. <br /> ST asks the question: &quot;Who murdered Mr. Stone?&quot;<br /> Player Character casts &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; to gain &quot;informed&quot;, and resolves it to get the answer. <br /> <br /> Unlike other divinatory spells, I don't know of a way to shield against Exceptional Luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:23:41-08:00","id":1156542,"title":"","content":"By causing circumstances to only give a piece of the information. If the player tries to give his character the condition again say that it doesn't work, even go so far as to have Fate snap back upon the mage.<br /> <br /> edit: I mean, this IS a storytelling game after all. If players demand to just jump to the conclusion then you shouldn't play with someone like that, no matter how they may argue that &quot;the rules&quot; are on their side. This is a cooperative experience, not spotlight #s21-100 all focused on Fate mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 11-06-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:40:31-08:00","id":1156547,"title":"","content":"Right, so regarding the point of exceptional luck not infinite, it still is super potent In buffing spellcasting, and stopping it otherwise requires some house-ruling to limit it from being otherwise exceptionally potent. And it would do so in a fashion that does seem to be a particularly strident case per RAW and ambiguous RAI. <br /> <br /> That is still good to know, that there is an upper limit as written, and that one could reasonably house rule a solution with minimal effort and alteration. <br /> <br /> <br /> I do find moderate annoyance in Fate's ability to effectively request to skip most of the interesting bits of any mystery or investigation though. Need to find something or someone, get somewhere like the shadow, or convince someone to help you? Well, the Fate mage can do all that with unprecedented ease, combined with the benefit of not needing to affect anyone but himself with magic, sparring them the issue of a werewolf taking issue to their mind influence, or a geist not liking being harassed and spied on by their pet ghost. This is mostly just an aspect of nothing mundane really being able to slow a Fate mage down at all. Lack of evidence? Luck past it. Stubborn rival? Magically boost your dice pool through the roof and talk past them. Fight? You just happened to spill coffee on your shirt earlier and avoided it, and even if they press the issue, you've got an attack pool through the roof, great defence, and can just use shared fates to make punishing you an awful idea. The one arcana seems an acceptable solution to all problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":".  Spelling 11-06-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:59:13-08:00","id":1156551,"title":"","content":"You could just suggest your players not learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T20:31:51-08:00","id":1156560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156551#post1156551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just suggest your players not learn it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think that's what I or anyone else are wanting. Fate is such an amazingly witchy arcanum and I would hate to lose it from Mage. I just struggle with how to rule on a few of its spells. I am enjoying listening to all the suggestions offered here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T20:34:11-08:00","id":1156561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156536#post1156536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player Character casts &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; to gain &quot;informed&quot;, and resolves it to get the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Said it before and I'll say it again:<br /> <br /> That's not how Informed works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who killed Mister Stone?&quot; is not going to be a roll-based question. You get a lucky lead on your Investigation roll and find an especially valuable piece of evidence (or find a single remaining scrap of evidence amid a veritable desert of clues) that points you in the right direction, just as you would a mundanely lucky roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156547#post1156547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find moderate annoyance in Fate's ability to effectively request to skip most of the interesting bits of any mystery or investigation though. [\u2026]. The one arcana seems an acceptable solution to all problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relying exclusively on Fate all but assures that you're going into most situations blind and drawing potential complications into your metaphysical orbit to get out of the trouble that doing so got you into. Keep track of what happens to let the character circumvent given obstacles and extrapolate bigger issues where they can fit. Fate isn't going to immediately help with extradimensional threats, counterspells, the Long-Term Nimbus, spell control, Paradox, or plain lack of foresight. The ST's job is to make the PCs' lives complicated and Fate is a blank checkbook to bring in weird shit on the bridges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T20:41:37-08:00","id":1156563,"title":"","content":"Fate works best in the hands of actually skilled people, whether in mundane or Supernal technique. Without a foundation, you'll stretch probability too thin and invite kinks into your machinations. It's a good thing to look at how the Enchanter archetype is looked at sometimes, which is to say, as a Magician who often ends up at their goal worse for wear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T21:41:57-08:00","id":1156576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156561#post1156561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said it before and I'll say it again:<br /> <br /> That's not how Informed works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who killed Mister Stone?&quot; is not going to be a roll-based question. You get a lucky lead on your Investigation roll and find an especially valuable piece of evidence (or find a single remaining scrap of evidence amid a veritable desert of clues) that points you in the right direction, just as you would a mundanely lucky roll.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T22:13:32-08:00","id":1156581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156563#post1156563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate works best in the hands of actually skilled people, whether in mundane or Supernal technique. Without a foundation, you'll stretch probability too thin and invite kinks into your machinations. It's a good thing to look at how the Enchanter archetype is looked at sometimes, which is to say, as a Magician who often ends up at their goal worse for wear.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for this detail I do feel inclined to disagree. (As I seem to do with every point on here. Sorry, obsessive Devil's Advocte trying to catch all The issues I might encounter or arguments I might hear in one go.) The input on exceptional luck's limits and potential alterations has been helpful, and the idea of introducing appropriately justified narrative complications a good one. However, when it comes to needing to be skilled or be stretched too thin, I feel that is incorrect. When it comes to accomplishing non-spellcasting goals, fate is very arguably the best, not only due to how it can have narrative influence, but also due to granting conditions, all with minimal effort low to no-cost spells. <br /> <br /> Unless I misunderstood, which is very plausible. I spend so much time be contrarian it can be hard for me to notice at times, and hard for people to tell that I don't actually dislike the Arcana <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Were you instead just suggesting the ST slap the Fate mage with &quot;bad times&quot; intermittently, the justification being their use of fate magic? I suppose I can see value in that, but am not *entirely* comfortable with the idea of ST fiated punishments out of the blue for a mage using magic. <br /> <br /> I suppose Fate, being the fiat arcana, sorta justifies that though lol. At least with spirits or ghosts or time magic you can kinda point to a reason and chain if logic or effect, whereas with fate it would just seem to kinda happen, without easily discernable cause. That latter point was my sticking point. Still, sound enough idea, if used with care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":". 11-07-2017, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T22:32:16-08:00","id":1156582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156581#post1156581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I can see value in that, but am not *entirely* comfortable with the idea of ST fiated punishments out of the blue for a mage using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put it this way:<br /> <br /> Even outside the context of it being the ST's explicit job to make things complicated for the players, the natural arc of an average Mage character is delving into magic and the Mysteries too deeply and/or too often and having to handle the ensuing dilemma brought on by awareness of a dozen fresh plates to keep spinning on a limited budget.<br /> <br /> The Fate Arcanum <i>distills </i>this phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Fate reveals the viability of routes between destinations, but skipping nine of ten steps can take you through strange country, and sometimes the locals take notice. Lean too heavily on serendipity to get werewolves to help you through the Shadow and you may find yourself dealing with the consequences of that entanglement \u2014 you may not have cast a spell on anyone but yourself at the start, but the limits of plausibility make it pretty unlikely that you'll get through that relationship without building up spiritual sympathies that take more specialized tools to get rid of. There's a reason &quot;set the course of events so that the exact thing I want to happen happens and was going to happen organically with no nasty side-effects stemming from the spell itself&quot; is the stuff of archmagic.<br /> <br /> (something something if a butterfly flaps its wings)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:25:25-08:00","id":1156612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156582#post1156582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put it this way:<br /> <br /> Even outside the context of it being the ST's explicit job to make things complicated for the players, the natural arc of an average Mage character is delving into magic and the Mysteries too deeply and/or too often and having to handle the ensuing dilemma brought on by awareness of a dozen fresh plates to keep spinning on a limited budget.<br /> <br /> The Fate Arcanum <i>distills </i>this phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Fate reveals the viability of routes between destinations, but skipping nine of ten steps can take you through strange country, and sometimes the locals take notice. Lean too heavily on serendipity to get werewolves to help you through the Shadow and you may find yourself dealing with the consequences of that entanglement \u2014 you may not have cast a spell on anyone but yourself at the start, but the limits of plausibility make it pretty unlikely that you'll get through that relationship without building up spiritual sympathies that take more specialized tools to get rid of. There's a reason &amp;quot;set the course of events so that the exact thing I want to happen happens and was going to happen organically with no nasty side-effects stemming from the spell itself&amp;quot; is the stuff of archmagic.<br /> <br /> (something something if a butterfly flaps its wings)</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. It's not a mattet of making them fail, but rather showing them how little they really understand about the predicament they're breezing by. My main character is a Master of Fate who rarely uses it beyond the immediate, knowing the possibility of things spinning out of his control can be all too easy without careful planning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T04:30:35-08:00","id":1156629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156581#post1156581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least with spirits or ghosts or time magic you can kinda point to a reason and chain if logic or effect, whereas with fate it would just seem to kinda happen, without easily discernable cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the ST your job is to make the chain of logic between a player's actions and their consequences crystal clear. If you can think of a complication that occurs because a player uses Fate to take the short cut, you should let them know in your narration that what's happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T09:34:07-08:00","id":1158516,"title":"","content":"I like all that stuff. Especially the things about the consequences of skipping steps and just arriving at answers/locations/places because &quot;Destiny told me so...&quot; This was a huge flaw in one of my favorite characters in that she had complete faith in her Fate and Time magic and was stubborn...<br /> <br /> But as an aside...<br /> <br /> This sort of topic comes up all the time with every Arcanum, right? Where the original poster sets up the perfect hypothetical situation in which they can amass whatever dice rolls they want in order to demonstrate that the Arcanum is broken and overpowered, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T10:13:57-08:00","id":1158535,"title":"","content":"It never happens with Matter. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Edit: Or Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T11:06:19-08:00","id":1158561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1158535#post1158535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never happens with Matter. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Edit: Or Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not here but i have seen arguments over using Aegis as a starting character to give yourself 8 general armor + mage armor for 11 general armor. A lot of people were adamant that no mage would go that far when infact its not even that hard to do. <br /> <br /> There is also the infamous &quot;Kinetic Shield&quot; creative thaum spell that gets argued over all the time on other sites, its broken and overpower or not depending on whoever is arguing about it at the time.<br /> <br /> There was a flaming argument over Prime being OP and the best Arcana the other day which was amusing, again not here.<br /> <br /> So yeh i think i have seen every Arcana portrayed as OP or broken now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:32:26-08:00","id":1158617,"title":"","content":"Lesson of the day: Mages are powerful. LOL<br /> <br /> My experience with the 2e so far over 13 sessions in the last 11 months is that you almost have to emphasize story and Wisdom consequences or the game could easily get out of hand.<br /> <br /> Mages make really good Murder Hobbos (see D&amp;D for reference) when starting characters can make themselves essentially immune to bullets with Matter.<br /> <br /> Any Adept with a skill of 3 in their Rote Lethal damage spell can get a dice pool of 3+4+3+3 (WP) = 13 - 8 (+4 potency) = 5 dice, use a Reach to target a whole cabal and a Reach for instant and sensory = 3 Reach, over Reaching by 1 = 2 paradox dice -&gt; chance die with a dedicated tool, and do 8 lethal in the first 6 seconds of combat to an entire cabal.<br /> <br /> So you don't have to get too far into the game before talking to a Mage is a lot better idea than fighting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:05:52-08:00","id":1158629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1158617#post1158617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesson of the day: Mages are powerful. LOL<br /> <br /> My experience with the 2e so far over 13 sessions in the last 11 months is that you almost have to emphasize story and Wisdom consequences or the game could easily get out of hand.<br /> <br /> Mages make really good Murder Hobbos (see D&amp;D for reference) when starting characters can make themselves essentially immune to bullets with Matter.<br /> <br /> Any Adept with a skill of 3 in their Rote Lethal damage spell can get a dice pool of 3+4+3+3 (WP) = 13 - 8 (+4 potency) = 5 dice, use a Reach to target a whole cabal and a Reach for instant and sensory = 3 Reach, over Reaching by 1 = 2 paradox dice -&gt; chance die with a dedicated tool, and do 8 lethal in the first 6 seconds of combat to an entire cabal.<br /> <br /> So you don't have to get too far into the game before talking to a Mage is a lot better idea than fighting one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless somebody in the other cabal counters it first :P<br /> <br /> But yeh while i have yet to have any exp with 2e (boooo) in my 1e campaign that ran long enough campaign for the players to all become at least second degree masters a lot of the stories revolved less about could they do something (almost always a yes) and more should they do something (almost always no). The consequences of powerful actions or spells should have equally powerful repercussions and as long as the threats and challenges, even just moral ones keep apace with the characters power level you can still have a fun and interesting game.<br /> <br /> I mean at the end of the campaign the characters had decided that the only way they could stop the actual prince of 100,000 leaves was to compile the entire thing themselves (or find a copy of it in the underworld dominion called the Athenaeum...) and then have it eaten by a logophage, which one character had to become (duh). By this point i certainly wasnt throwing murder mystery stories at them because i knew they would solve them in 5 minutes.<br /> <br /> tldr, Agree with Johnny, Consquences should happen at any powerlevel, and you shouldnt feel afraid to let your PC's let rip once in awhile because there will always be something or somebody who may want to change whatever the players do and they too are probably OP mages or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-14-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:30:14-08:00","id":1158988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1158617#post1158617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with the 2e so far over 13 sessions in the last 11 months is that you almost have to emphasize story and Wisdom consequences or the game could easily get out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a rule in my Mage game that all 'planning sessions' and conversations about the Cabals actions take place IC. Its occasionally a bit of a culture shock for players more used to DnD, but I find it really adds to games like Mage, where finding the elegant solution to a specific problem is usually the focus. Emphasising dealing with the fallout of their choices and witnessing the impacts of 'less elegant' solutions is also worthwhile (and again should be done IC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:35:42-08:00","id":1158997,"title":"","content":"I like it in principle, but two of my 3 players are 10 and 12 years old, so harder to achieve for my play group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:44:22-08:00","id":1159000,"title":"","content":"I can imagine it is! Props to you though sir. As a teacher myself I wouldnt envy running something as complex as Mage with younger kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:06:43-08:00","id":1161297,"title":"","content":"I banned Steadfast (automatic successes? Not in my game) and forbidden Fate to give dice bonuses on spellcasting rolls (but allowed to give 9 and 8-again). So far it works, but mostly because player with Fate never ever uses it (because he have no idea how to do that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:14:34-08:00","id":1161302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1161297#post1161297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I banned Steadfast (automatic successes? Not in my game) and forbidden Fate to give dice bonuses on spellcasting rolls (but allowed to give 9 and 8-again). So far it works, but mostly because player with Fate never ever uses it (because he have no idea how to do that).</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you handle Informed? It doesn't work with spellcasting as written anyway, but if you're opposed to the idea of automatic successes in general, I'm curious how you handle it.<br /> <br /> What about other merits or effects that grant them (whether literally, or for all practical purposes?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:40:56-08:00","id":1161497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1156353#post1156353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are Fate effects that counter mind control effects as they impede your \u201cdestiny\u201d as determined by your own will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the fourth dot attainment, not a spell if you are talking about the Clash of Will against supernatural affecting your destiny. I would note Life grants a similar Clash of Wills against all supernatural changes to your body, which includes supernatural sources of damage, and Spirit allows you to have Honorary Spirit rank at that level, and Forces allow you to skip and dance in a tornado without even casting a spell at that level for a single point of Mana. That's the bar of power at that level of Arcana mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:54:50-08:00","id":1161502,"title":"","content":"Check out the 2 dot spell for fate warding gesture. That's the spell that is counter Mind control since it includes Mind control as a thing that messes with the destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:07:11-08:00","id":1161508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11759\" data-vbnamecard=\"11759\">Bonreu</a> said, and it\u2019s not the only effect, Sworn Oaths for instance is another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T06:27:39-08:00","id":1161841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bonreu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1161502#post1161502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out the 2 dot spell for fate warding gesture. That's the spell that is counter Mind control since it includes Mind control as a thing that messes with the destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1161508#post1161508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11759\" data-vbnamecard=\"11759\">Bonreu</a> said, and it\u2019s not the only effect, Sworn Oaths for instance is another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderful points! I did not see that, thank you both for letting me know about that.<br /> <br /> Thought: Wouldn't the fact the 4 dot Attainment of Fate be something they can accomplish via a 2 dot spell mean the primary real benefit of the 4 dot Attainment amounts to freeing up a single spell control slot, as opposed to the other new defensive and utility abilities other Arcana Attainments grant at that level? (Rhetorical)<br /> <br /> I mean even a potently cast shielding Forces spell lacks the power of the Forces 4 dot Attainment has.<br /> <br /> Sworn Oaths has the narrative effect defending the target that in stories Fate tends to enforce Oaths so it is possible for the following link to apply as a standard for the target's behavior:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/JackassGenie\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/JackassGenie</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-23-2017, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:08:16-08:00","id":1161920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1161841#post1161841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thought: Wouldn't the fact the 4 dot Attainment of Fate be something they can accomplish via a 2 dot spell mean the primary real benefit of the 4 dot Attainment amounts to freeing up a single spell control slot, as opposed to the other new defensive and utility abilities other Arcana Attainments grant at that level? (Rhetorical)<br /> <br /> I mean even a potently cast shielding Forces spell lacks the power of the Forces 4 dot Attainment has.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh alot of them are like that. I mean the Death 4 attainment replicates a 2dot spell. The effects of the life 2 attainment might be replicated with a 2dot life spell though that is debatable. The Forces 4 Attainment definitly could be replicated with a shielding spell, environmental shield namely.<br /> <br /> The ones that stick out as something more interesting than a freedup spell slot (and being undispellable I guess.. but you clash dicepool is worse than it would be with a spell so nyeh) are Time and Space. (Mind, Matter etc could again be done with a spell and vastly better at that)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:22:22-08:00","id":1161925,"title":"","content":"While MtA only says spells gain bonuses from longer duration, most of the other second edition core books states that the duration bonuses apply to all supernatural powers. The always on Attainments should get +4 in CoWs. Spells can only get one more die due to Advanced Potency, which is by far the least used standard Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:27:23-08:00","id":1161928,"title":"","content":"The 4th dot &quot;defense&quot; attainments typically have a slightly broader range of application than any one spell can manage on its own, or some other special condition. Fate for instance allows you to CoW in an instance where Warding Gesture doesn't, specifically, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This spell has no effect on pre-existing alterations to<br /> the subject\u2019s destiny. </div> </div> </div> Which is pretty niche, and another niche effect it also protects you from the trick clause of Sworn Oaths and other such powers, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She is being forcibly bound into a magical oath, contract, or geas. </div> </div> </div> which none of the other printed spells do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:44:50-08:00","id":1162008,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that an attainment will protect you always, and won't ping as magical iirc(at very least while not in use), but is limited to yourself. The spell lets you protect others, and like warding gesture has another feature to it in the form of exempting the target from your other spells. They each have their own uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:20:44-08:00","id":1162073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1161297#post1161297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I banned Steadfast (automatic successes? Not in my game) and forbidden Fate to give dice bonuses on spellcasting rolls (but allowed to give 9 and 8-again). So far it works, but mostly because player with Fate never ever uses it (because he have no idea how to do that).</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, i understand some people like the narrative snowball approach. &quot;This power seems OP but is the DM responsibility to DM fiat it to have consequences&quot; which, to each their own i guess.<br /> <br /> I am not a fan, in my experience it always leaves a bitter taste on the players mouth with their reasoning being &quot;why punish me for using a power that you allow me to buy with consequences that arent in the description?&quot;. And it generates (in my experience) a derailment problem. So player A does uses X power but I, the DM, make the situation more complicated for it to have consequences which is gonna derail the main plot with them dealing with it. But then Player B also uses X spell or similar Y spell, now I gotta keep derailing the game with consequences within consequences or i can just say that Player B cast and we continue but then, player A gets angry because he felt single out for a house rule which is basically DM-Fiat the rule.<br /> <br /> This is also why I am not a fan of touchstones and vice/virtue equivalents for splats.<br /> <br /> Before doing that i prefer to nerf the whole arcanum to manageable levels and then (the players) using it at their hearts content but i am a mechanics oriented person more than a narrative on the fly one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T21:42:59-08:00","id":1162092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155342-i-m-worried-that-the-fate-arcana-is-too-potent-whether-mechanically-or-narratively?p=1158629#post1158629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tldr, Agree with Johnny, Consquences should happen at any powerlevel, and you shouldnt feel afraid to let your PC's let rip once in awhile because there will always be something or somebody who may want to change whatever the players do and they too are probably OP mages or similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, in my opinion, &quot;the answer&quot; to the dilemma posed by OP: The PCs may well be able to thwart any obstacle you define in static terms, so instead, oppose them with obstacles that are as versatile as they are. Having problems with a Fate mage abusing the Arcanum? Sic a Time mage who knows the ins-and-outs of manipulating history on 'em, or a Prime mage with an expertise in reading and countering reality-unravelling effects, or a Space/Mind mage who can hit them from afar while manipulating the ability of their target to even perceive their imminent assault.<br /> <br /> After all, if your Fate mage is so powerful that he or she is giving YOU, as the Storyteller (and ostensible God of the whole game) any real concern... then you obviously have sufficient justification to say that same character is earning attention from some very powerful NPCs.<br /> <br /> TL,DR: There's always a bigger fish in the sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}